{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/related_block

    What the [relatedcourses] shortcode prints (local\related\shortcode): for a reader who may edit the
    text, a notice naming what the shortcode refers to and this site lacks; then the related courses band,
    when there is a course to list. The root carries theme_dimensions-related, the second root of the
    landing page's stylesheet (scss/landing.scss), so the band is drawn as on a landing page on any page
    the theme draws.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * notice - Core's warning notification's context (message already escaped, no close button), or null.
    * band - The related_band context, or null.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "notice": {"message": "The related courses shortcode refers to what this site does not have: framework FW09.", "closebutton": false, "announce": false},
        "band": {
            "region": "dimensions-related-block",
            "cards": [
                {"courseid": 51, "name": "Advanced Life Support", "url": "https://example.com/theme/dimensions/landing.php?id=51", "imageurl": null, "category": "Emergency care", "hours": "40 hours"}
            ],
            "count": 1
        }
    }
}}
<div class="theme_dimensions-related" data-region="dimensions-related">
    {{#notice}}
        {{> core/notification_warning }}
    {{/notice}}
    {{#band}}
        {{> theme_dimensions/related_band }}
    {{/band}}
</div>
